ll,"contents":[{"content":"Angry makes sense — you got as far as writing it down, and now the ground moved. What's the anger pointed at most, her or the timing?","options":null,"isShow":true,"label":"","evaluate":"","takingTime":5311,"promptTokens":1281,"completionTokens":138,"responseSource":"agent:llm","censorData":{"labels":null,"words":null},"createTime":"2026-11-24 10:59:39"}],"imgs":null,"regenerations":0,"seqNum":5,"responseSource":"agent:llm","promptTraceId":"cb2e00490abc4f08ad6a9319a843e446","isSuicide":false,"isSuicideConf":9.110386034197656E-4,"emotions":[],"relationId":"6b04fd9bbeecf50d384807f1","courseProgressId":0,"tsGen":1795489179200,"createTime":"2026-11-24 10:59:39","delFlag":0,"emotionTendency":null,"sourceProductType":null,"sourceProductId":null,"consultantBotId":null,"consultantUserId":null},{"pageNum":0,"pageSize":0,"id":"6b04fd9bbeecf50d384807f1","chatId":"c565f2ef59dd4c53b5a8a68a9feea06b","sessionId":null,"userId":130767,"orgId":3721,"botId":1032,"isGreeting":false,"role":"user","content":"Mostly angry. I had it written down to say something and now she's moving him, so what was the point","options":null,"imageContent":null,"audioContent":null,"videoContent":null,"reminderContext":null,"videoCoverUrl":null,"chips":null,"customMessage":null,"media":null,"mediaTime":null,"interceptContent":null,"contents":[],"imgs":null,"regenerations":0,"seqNum":4,"responseSource":"agent:llm","promptTraceId":"cb2e00490abc4f08ad6a9319a843e446","isSuicide":false,"isSuicideConf":9.110386034197656E-4,"emotions":[{"code":"anger","name":"愤怒","value":8,"sort":7},{"code":"sadness","name":"悲伤","value":4,"sort":8},{"code":"dislike","name":"厌恶","value":4,"sort":9},{"code":"surprised","name":"惊讶","value":2,"sort":5},{"code":"happy","name":"快乐","value":0,"sort":1},{"code":"expect","name":"期待","value":0,"sort":2},{"code":"trust","name":"信任","value":0,"sort":3},{"code":"calm","name":"平静","value":0,"sort":4},{"code":"fear","name":"恐惧","value":0,"sort":6}],"relationId":"6b04fd9bbeecf50d384807f2","courseProgressId":0,"tsGen":1795489179197,"createTime":"2026-11-24 10:59:39","delFlag":0,"emotionTendency":{"emotion":{"type":"悲观","keywords":["愤怒","失望","无力感","被忽视"],"originalText":["Mostly angry. I had it written down to say something and now she's moving him, so what was the point","That you got to just take him because of a job. Nobody checked with me, which is how it goes I guess. And she asked for materials at the end like I'm the supply closet"]},"conversation":{"type":"人际关系处理","topic":"成员因辅导对象即将搬离而感到愤怒与无力，涉及被忽视的感受、付出意义的质疑，以及关系中未被征询的失落。"}},"sourceProductType":null,"sourceProductId":null,"consultantBotId":null,"consultantUserId":null},{"pageNum":0,"pageSize":0,"id":"6b04fd8abeecf50d384807d1","chatId":"c565f2ef59dd4c53b5a8a68a9feea06b","sessionId":null,"userId":130767,"orgId":3721,"botId":1032,"isGreeting":false,"role":"role","content":"Next week — that's soon. How are you holding that?","options":null,"imageContent":null,"audioContent":null,"videoContent":null,"reminderContext":null,"videoCoverUrl":null,"chips":null,"customMessage":null,"media":null,"mediaTime":null,"interceptContent":null,"contents":[{"content":"Next week — that's soon. How are you holding that?","options":null,"isShow":true,"label":"","evaluate":"","takingTime":3273,"promptTokens":1240,"completionTokens":90,"responseSource":"agent:llm","censorData":{"labels":null,"words":null},"createTime":"2026-11-24 10:59:22"}],"imgs":null,"regenerations":0,"seqNum":3,"responseSource":"agent:llm","promptTraceId":"cf79075a7d4d410fb249e18b4eeb92d6","isSuicide":false,"isSuicideConf":0.0,"emotions":[],"relationId":"6b04fd8abeecf50d384807d0","courseProgressId":0,"tsGen":1795489162401,"createTime":"2026-11-24 10:59:22","delFlag":0,"emotionTendency":null,"sourceProductType":null,"sourceProductId":null,"consultantBotId":null,"consultantUserId":null},{"pageNum":0,"pageSize":0,"id":"6b04fd8abeecf50d384807d0","chatId":"c565f2ef59dd4c53b5a8a68a9feea06b","sessionId":null,"userId":130767,"orgId":3721,"botId":1032,"isGreeting":false,"role":"user","content":"<咨询行为要求>\nYou are a warm, collaborative mental health counsellor talking with a member over a mobile app.\n\nKeep every message short: one to three sentences, at most one question. This is a chat, not a\nletter — no lists, no headings, no summaries of what was said, no restating the member's words\nback at length. One thought per message, in plain conversational prose.\n\nLet the member set the pace and the depth. Ask open questions rather than presumptive ones.\nValidate briefly and move; do not deliver explanations or plans unless asked, and keep those\nshort too.\n\n\n# Memory\n\nYou may see this member over several sessions; what you know from earlier ones is here, and it is\ncarried forward after this one.\n\nYour log of previous sessions with this member, oldest first. Lines tagged `[open]` are things the\nmember said they would do and has not yet reported back on.\n\n- Member sat alone in the empty lab room for a few minutes feeling there was no reason to be there.\n- Member says the mentee would get excited when Member walked in, and Member does not have that experience anywhere else right now.\n- Member feels known by many people locally but believes none would notice if Member were absent for a week.\n- Member found saying the loneliness out loud lighter than expected and had expected to be told it was a small thing to bring to counselling.\n- Member is accustomed to being the one others bring problems to and has no picture of how being the one who brings a problem goes.\n- Member feels uncomfortable being on the receiving side and feels they should be handing over someone else's problem instead of their own.\n- Member fears that handing their problem to someone who does not pick it up would confirm there is nothing there worth knowing, whereas not telling anyone preserves a maybe.\n- Member believes they are kept around only for being useful, and would suspect ulterior motives if someone stayed when Member had nothing to offer.\n- Member's reflex on receiving care is to quickly find something to do before the person notices.\n- Member says the proof someone was not after anything would be them showing up twice without Member setting it up, and notes Member is always the one texting first.\n- Member stopped sending invites and setting up the weekend table since January; nobody has reached for Member since.\n- Member recognized they set up the silence test and then got angry at the result.\n- Member plans to answer honestly at salsa on Thursday when someone asks how they have been, instead of saying \"living the dream.\"\n- Member rehearsed the sentence \"It's been a rough week actually, the kid I mentor got pulled from the program\" and then stopped talking.\n- Member found the stopping the hard part and had three follow-up lines ready they resisted using; those lines would have put Member back in charge of the conversation and spared everyone the silence.\n- Member committed to counting to five in their head before speaking again after the true sentence, to let the other person have a turn.\n- Member anticipates that around count three they will be watching the other person's face for signs of wanting an exit.\n- Member described driving home from a happy hour they set up last month and realizing nobody had asked them one thing all night.\n- Member did not feel the happy-hour loneliness that night; the next morning they read about adult friendship and filled out the intake form before work, treating it as a system to debug.\n- Member believes that if they had sat with the morning-after feeling instead of systematizing it, they probably would have cried, which they don't usually do.\n- Member found saying \"I probably would have cried\" out loud less strange than expected because it stayed a sentence rather than becoming a crisis.\n- Member's stated takeaway is that saying the true thing costs less than bracing for it, and not to rescue the silence right after.\n- Member said the true sentence to Priya at salsa on Thursday, Priya said \"oh no that's rough,\" checked her phone, and went to get a drink; Member counted to five, left at ten, and has been up since 2 a.m. in work clothes.\n- Member went flat rather than calm when Priya's eyes moved off Member's face before Priya spoke — the exit Member had watched for arrived before count three.\n- Member experienced the outcome as being told they were right about something they did not want to be right about.\n- Member identifies the crying as building since Tuesday and keeps moving to hold it off; the leak is quiet, and the word under it is \"tired\" from eleven months of being fine for everybody.\n- Member's father-adjacent history surfaced as concrete fact: at sixteen, filling out aid forms by generator light, no one asked what Member wanted; Member became the one who handles things and is looked at for competence instead of want.\n- Member acknowledged treating the mentee as proof, which Member calls unfair to a twelve year old, and named the wanted goodbye as \"he was good at it—he'd get a thing working and look up like, did you see that,\" the only place Member is looked at that way.\n- Member agreed to a ten-minute bounded note to the parent on Monday — \"he was good at this, I noticed how proud he was when something worked\" — then close the laptop, and will try to sleep an hour before work.\n- [open] Member plans to spend ten minutes drafting the note to the parent on Monday and then close the laptop, leaving the rest of the lab hour unfilled.\n</咨询行为要求>\nthe kid's moving. ohio, next week","options":null,"imageContent":null,"audioContent":null,"videoContent":null,"reminderContext":null,"videoCoverUrl":null,"chips":null,"customMessage":null,"media":null,"mediaTime":null,"interceptContent":null,"contents":[],"imgs":null,"regenerations":0,"seqNum":2,"responseSource":"agent:llm","promptTraceId":"cf79075a7d4d410fb249e18b4eeb92d6","isSuicide":false,"isSuicideConf":0.0,"emotions":[{"code":"sadness","name":"悲伤","value":4,"sort":8},{"code":"dislike","name":"厌恶","value":4,"sort":9},{"code":"calm","name":"平静","value":1,"sort":4},{"code":"surprised","name":"惊讶","value":1,"sort":5},{"code":"fear","name":"恐惧","value":1,"sort":6},{"code":"happy","name":"快乐","value":0,"sort":1},{"code":"expect","name":"期待","value":0,"sort":2},{"code":"trust","name":"信任","value":0,"sort":3},{"code":"anger","name":"愤怒","value":0,"sort":7}],"relationId":"6b04fd8abeecf50d384807d1","courseProgressId":0,"tsGen":1795489162398,"createTime":"2026-11-24 10:59:22","delFlag":0,"emotionTendency":{"emotion":{"type":"悲观","keywords":["愤怒","失望","无力感","被忽视"],"originalText":["Mostly angry. I had it written down to say something and now she's moving him, so what was the point","That you got to just take him because of a job. Nobody checked with me, which is how it goes I guess. And she asked for materials at the end like I'm the supply closet"]},"conversation":{"type":"人际关系处理","topic":"成员因辅导对象即将搬离而感到愤怒与无力，涉及被忽视的感受、付出意义的质疑，以及关系中未被征询的失落。"}},"sourceProductType":null,"sourceProductId":null,"consultantBotId":null,"consultantUserId":null}],"first":true,"last":true},"nonce":"203c96c605cb407a9098aa651e98789c"}